what's the last thing anyone expected to  see in the first episode of she-hulk how  about busted tech from mcu phase two  here's the history behind the surprising  memento the marvel cinematic universe  has thrilled audiences on the big and  small screen for more than a decade and  in all that time there's only been one  in-universe version of the hulk bruce  banner was originally played by edward  norton in the incredible hulk before  mark ruffalo came aboard for the  avengers but it's the same character in  the mcu however the hero has been joined  by a brand new jade giant jennifer  walters also known as she-hulk played by  tatiana maslany of orphan black fame jen  gets her powers from bruce's blood when  they get into a car accident due to a  sicarian ship showing up out of nowhere  a seeming nod to the world war hulk  comics the series kicks things off by  establishing a fun dynamic between the  two cousins as professor hulk tries to  teach jen everything there is to know  about being a hulk speaking to access  hollywood in february ruffalo had high  praise for maslany freaking legendary as  a she-hulk um i'm passing the banner  onto her ruffalo added there are some  really good funny cool long long scenes  between professor and her we've never  really seen the hulk interact with  people the way he does in that show  it'll be really interesting bruce and  jen spend plenty of time in the isolated  mexican laboratory where the scientist  learned to merge his two selves in the  time between avengers infinity war and  avengers end game but when walters is  wandering around the building she finds  a bittersweet iron man memento that has  us all in our feelings here's why it's  so familiar although she-hulk is  obviously about jennifer walters and how  she balances her legal career alongside  her burgeoning responsibilities as a  superhero the show also takes the  opportunity to look at bruce banner a  little more closely episode one reveals  that bruce spent a lot of time with tony  stark in the five-year blip gap after  avengers infinity war because the  billionaire playboy philanthropist  funded his laboratory they even built a  beachside bar together to have some fun  even in a dramatic time but bruce seems  to have done more of the work than his  pal  tony mostly drank just sat around  complaining about steve when jen is  wandering through the house she finds a  ruined iron man helmet that bruce is  clearly keeping to remember his fallen  friend it seems like the black and gold  helmet could be from a mark 20 python  suit which briefly shows up with several  other suits at the end of iron man 3.  fans will remember that bruce briefly  appears in the post-credits scene of the  2013 movie nodding off while listening  to tony ramble on but the mark 20 suit  blows up on tony's orders after the  final big battle in iron man 3. so it's  way more likely that the memento is  actually an iron legion droid head from  the avengers age of ultron era these  unwearable suits were ultimately used  against the avengers when ultron who was  developed with bruce's help took control  of them this little memento reminds us  that tony and bruce had a real  friendship that thrived outside of  saving the world when the two first meet  in the avengers tony tells bruce that  he's a big fan of his especially when he  grows into an enormous green rage  monster over the years we see them  connect and grow as friends working on  projects and driving around in supercars  together using a small part of she-hulk  attorney at law to look a little closer  at hulk's character arc is a clever move  from marvel after all the giant hero  hasn't had his own solo movie since 2008  since the distribution rights for the  character are universal so any mcu hulk  action is a welcome turn of events even  on the small screen  [Music]
 

